          "note": "Hard constraint c02: 'Applied half-timbering is forbidden. The variant is defined by its absence; a single timbered panel returns the building to tudor-revival.' The inherited value from tudor-revival is exactly this variant's defining reversal."
        }
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "parapet_rise_min": {
          "value": 12,
          "unit": "in",
          "kind": "measured",
          "note": "c01."
        },
        "coping_thickness_min": {
          "value": 6,
          "unit": "in",
          "kind": "measured",
          "note": "c01."
        }
      },
      "rule": "Gables on principal elevations are parapeted -- straight with copings and finials, or shaped in curvilinear Flemish-derived profiles -- never half-timbered and never a raking eave with a bargeboard.",
      "confidence": "high",
      "note": "Overrides tudor-revival's half-timbered/parapeted-forbidden binding outright: this variant exists specifically as the parapeted, all-masonry reversal of that rule.",
